# The change-brief render pipeline is POSIX shell/awk that rejects CRLF
# input outright (see render.sh's explicit CRLF guards). Pin these files to
# LF so a contributor cloning with core.autocrlf=true does not get a
# checkout that git itself has silently made unrenderable.
assets/change-brief/template.html text eol=lf
assets/change-brief/render.sh text eol=lf
assets/change-brief/scan.awk text eol=lf
assets/change-brief/tests/render_test.sh text eol=lf
assets/change-brief/tests/fixtures/*.md text eol=lf
# The same guard, applied to the real render inputs. `render.sh` rejects a CRLF
# spec or plan by name and exits 1, so an unpinned `docs/` markdown file is the
# one way a clean checkout still cannot render its own brief.
docs/specs/*.md text eol=lf
docs/plans/*.md text eol=lf
